// Subject: the game's damage model and authored presentation; game state only.
// The spall cone's shape and its potency — the field thrown from every body exit a round
// reaches —, and a burst's field. Read by `src/ballistics/spall_cone.rs`, embedded and parsed once,
// validated at parse.
// The law (emitted HP, the ball law's centre-weighted profile, shadowing, dose) is design doc
// §§5–6, `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`. A field carries the energy its
// source put into it (a cone its share of the energy its round lost at the plate, a burst its
// wall's driven energy), which a construction crushes with; each mechanism declares its own HP scale,
// which only a box's pool reads.
// A cone's half-angle and profile follow from its exit layer's debris ratio in
// `assets/materials/materials.ron`.
//
// Every value here is a choice the owner can change by editing this file alone; none is a
// constant of the law. The playtest fork on the axis is F5 in
// `.agents/scratch/playtest-forks/README.md`.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind names the value's job
// (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    // The cone's axis. `RearNormalBisector`: normalize(rear-face outward normal + exit direction)
    // at a genuine exit, the exit direction at an internal step (which has no face).
    // `ExitDirection`: the exit direction everywhere.
    axis: (RearNormalBisector, Unknown("ASSUMED engineering proxy (playtest fork F5) with MEASURED
        support: debris axis about halfway between the shot line and the plate normal, 25° measured
        against 22.5° predicted at 45° obliquity (Verolme 1997, Recht & Howell 1967;
        research/cloud-angle-deep.md). Settled by measured debris-axis directions across materials
        and obliquities")),

    // N, the number of directions the cone is sampled by, in equal-solid-angle strata of 1/N of the
    // cone each, every one weighted by its stratum's share of the field. The emitted total is S/2
    // at every N, so N changes how finely a box's dose is resolved, never how much the cone
    // carries.
    directions: (64, Resolution("owner decision 2026-10-17 ('64 for now'), the cost against the
        resolution: one throw under the ball law MEASURED 2026-10-24 by
        ballistics::pen_cam::spall_law_cost (release, macOS arm64, best of 9, the 7 cones of the
        penetrating scenarios): 0.30 ms at N = 24, 0.64 at 64, 1.23 at 128, 2.29 at 256; the dose
        step per direction on the s1 cone at 64 runs from 10.5 HP on the axis to 0.65 HP at the rim,
        6.25 HP on average (DERIVED from that historical record's 400 emitted HP:
        H_C·f_k / (q·N), q = 1/2, the field weights' exact normalization).
        The count changes how finely a box's dose is resolved, never the emitted total")),

    // κ: the share of the energy a round loses across a body that its debris carries out through
    // an exit of the reference steel's strength. A cone carries κ × the exit's strength ratio of
    // that energy and the line deals the body's volumes the rest, so the two spend it once; a
    // construction reads the cone's share as crushing energy. HP does not move with it (the unit below
    // is per joule lost).
    cone_debris_energy_share: (0.06, StandIn("missing law: debris production from the crossed
        construction and material. This global share and the capped exit resistance ratio used
        for emission together stand in for that law; resistance is not a debris-yield fact.
        Order of magnitude,
        DERIVED: a plug of the reference steel (7850 kg/m³, materials.ron) the 88 mm reference
        round's disc wide and its 100 mm reference plate thick, 4.774 kg, leaving at the round's
        259.69 m/s exit speed carries 161.0 kJ of the 2.7035 MJ the round lost, 0.0596, rounded.
        Replaced by construction- and material-dependent debris production, grounded in measured
        fragment masses and speeds against the energy the construction absorbed")),

    // HP per joule of the energy lost across the exited body, weighted by its material strength
    // ratio: a box's field dose is the joules a direction left there times this over κ, so the
    // cone's emitted HP is this × the ratio × the energy lost, whatever κ.
    // DERIVED: 0.88 × 1/2 / 3000, a fixed number of its own that no line unit moves.
    cone_emitted_hp_per_joule: (0.00014666666666666666, Unit("provisional HP calibration per joule
        lost at the plate; balance lives here. The runtime unit u_C / kappa preserves emitted HP
        as the debris share changes: this is calibration, not a physical debris-production law.
        Set against the retired reference cone's 395.0 HP target,
        rounded to the scale emitting 396.5 HP (DERIVED). Replaced by the missing fragment-hit law:
        fragments empty crew-station HP pools by hits rather than energy caught on a face. Design
        doc §§5–6, .agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md, owns the derivation")),

    // A burst's field (design doc §5a, "The burst"): thrown from the burst point about the round's
    // flight direction, its ratio the carried speed over the burst's greatest sideways speed v_s,
    // through spatially reached volumes, passing as the spall cone's directions do. Every burst
    // is a ring: the wall around the burst core is driven as a band about the flight axis, and the
    // nose piece flies on.
    burst: (
        // HP per joule of the energy a burst field carries, its wall's driven energy, independent
        // of the line and cone units. DERIVED: 210 × 1/2 / 3000, a fixed number of its own.
        emitted_hp_per_joule: (0.035, Unit("provisional emitted HP per joule driven into the wall;
            balance lives here. Set against the retired even-sphere target: a 0.2 m² face at 2.0 m
            has its 30 HP pool emptied. That target set the retired ball's scale (214.8 kJ driven,
            DERIVED); preserving the unit when the ring drives 397.7 kJ gives 13,920.84 emitted HP,
            DERIVED, rather than re-tuning the ring to that sphere target. Replaced by the
            missing fragment-hit law: fragments empty crew-station HP pools by hits rather than
            energy caught on a face. Design doc §§5–6,
            .agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md, owns the derivation")),
        // h (degrees): the ring spans θ_c − h to θ_c + h of polar angle from the flight axis,
        // θ_c = atan(1/λ), uniform over that band; its near edge is held at the axis.
        ring_half_width_deg: (10.0, Unknown("provisional (owner's brief 4b): the band the wall's
            fragments leave in, one datum for every ring. Settled by measured fragment angular
            spread for the declared casing construction")),
        // N for the ring, as `directions` is for the cone: the emitted total is S/2 at every N, so
        // N sets how finely a box's dose is resolved, never how much the burst carries. One
        // throw's cost MEASURED 2026-10-24 by ballistics::pen_cam::burst_law_cost (release, macOS
        // arm64, best of 9, s1's line fired with the burst round). At rest each direction carries
        // H_B / N emitted HP (DERIVED, the field uniform over its support). S/2 is the wall's
        // driven energy, the joules environment construction is struck with.
        ring_directions: (256, Resolution("provisional, flagged for the owner: the cost against the
            resolution. The ring's throw: 0.50 ms at N = 64, 1.47 at 256, 4.01 at 684; at rest 218,
            54 and 20 HP points per direction (DERIVED: H_B = 0.035 HP/J × 397.7 kJ, then
            H_B / N), so at 256 one direction is about two crew pools")),
    ),
)
